  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Pakistan 2024 &#x2013; Locally led dialogue sessions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan faces some of the highest disaster risk levels in the world. Because of its vulnerable socio-economic profile and multi-geographic positioning, the country is listed among those worst affected by extreme weather events due to climate change.The Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO), in the framework of the DRRS programme, intends to facilitate three dialogue sessions with civil society and government agencies on flood resilience in the Pakistani provinces of Baluchistan, Punjab and Sindh.Additionally, three dialogues will be organised at community level to capture insight on flood impact, flood resilience and preparedness, and the long-lasting impact of floods &#x2013; positive and negative.In doing so, the aim is to get a better understanding on flood preparedness and ways of raising resilience on a local level; to inform and mobilise key stakeholders and raise awareness amongst an even broader range of key stakeholders to unify thought and measures on increasing flood preparedness and resilience on a local level.</narrative>
  </description>
